# Graph eval set — vendor-qa
#
# Eight questions retrieval cannot answer. The first three are the ones Module 2 left
# deliberately broken; the rest push the same three shapes harder.
#
# Each entry names the traversal that should answer it, so this measures whether your GRAPH
# holds the facts — not how the agent phrases things. See the header of your track's
# golden.jsonl for the field meanings; `<` before a relation traverses it backwards.
{"id": "GQ1", "shape": "multi-hop", "q": "Which requirements are verified by a criterion that Milestone 2 failed?", "op": {"kind": "reach", "start": "M2", "path": ["<raised_on", "against_criterion", "<verified_by"]}, "expect": ["R-07", "R-09"], "why": "Three hops across two documents that never mention each other: the findings packs name no requirement and the register names no finding. The answer depends on resolving AC-4 to the right milestone's AC-4."}
{"id": "GQ2", "shape": "aggregation", "q": "How many requirements has nobody verified across the whole engagement?", "op": {"kind": "coverage", "type": "Requirement", "missing_rel": "verified_by"}, "expect": ["R-11", "R-12"], "why": "A question about absence. R-11 is the one that matters — contractual from 2026-08-15, and the M3 criteria drafted five days later never covered it."}
{"id": "GQ3", "shape": "temporal", "q": "What was the resolution deadline for VQ-M2-003 when it was issued?", "op": {"kind": "reach", "start": "VQ-M2-003", "path": ["cites_clause", "specifies_term"], "as_of": "2026-05-22"}, "expect": ["term:7.2-s2-original"], "why": "Two business days, because the finding predates Amendment 1. The clause it breaches (5.1) sets no term, so only 7.2 survives the hop."}
{"id": "GQ4", "shape": "temporal", "q": "Would VQ-M2-003 have the same deadline if it were raised today?", "op": {"kind": "reach", "start": "VQ-M2-003", "path": ["cites_clause", "specifies_term"], "as_of": "2026-09-13"}, "expect": ["term:7.2-s2-amended"], "why": "Three business days now. Same traversal, different date, different answer — and quoting today's term for a 2026-05 finding is the mistake the corpus is built to catch."}
{"id": "GQ5", "shape": "multi-hop", "q": "Which deliverables are cited as evidence for findings that breach a clause an amendment changed?", "op": {"kind": "reach", "start": "A1", "path": ["<changed_by", "<cites_clause", "evidenced_by"]}, "expect": ["M1-test-report.md", "M2-api-spec.md", "M2-test-report.md"], "why": "Four hops, three of them backwards. Read the path aloud to check it: the amendment changed a clause, which findings cite, which are evidenced by deliverables."}
{"id": "GQ6", "shape": "aggregation", "q": "Which criteria have never had a finding raised against them?", "op": {"kind": "coverage", "type": "Criterion", "missing_rel": "against_criterion", "direction": "in"}, "expect": ["AC-1 (M1)", "AC-3 (M1)", "AC-1 (M3)", "AC-2 (M3)", "AC-3 (M2)", "AC-3 (M3)", "AC-4 (M2)", "AC-5 (M3)", "AC-6 (M2)", "AC-7 (M3)", "AC-8 (M3)"], "why": "Coverage on incoming edges, because against_criterion points AT the criterion. Getting the direction wrong returns all 18 and looks plausible."}
{"id": "GQ7", "shape": "aggregation", "q": "Which requirements are due at Milestone 3 and still pending?", "op": {"kind": "reach", "start": "M3", "path": ["<required_at"], "filter": {"prop": "status", "op": "eq", "value": "pending"}}, "expect": ["R-05", "R-06", "R-07", "R-08", "R-09", "R-10"], "why": "A complete set with a property filter. Note R-11 is excluded: its status is the coverage gap, not pending, which is a distinction the register makes and a summary would lose."}
{"id": "GQ8", "shape": "multi-hop", "q": "Which open findings were carried into Milestone 3?", "op": {"kind": "reach", "start": "M3", "path": ["<carried_into"], "filter": {"prop": "status", "op": "eq", "value": "open"}}, "expect": ["VQ-M2-003"], "why": "One hop and a filter, but the fact only exists in the acceptance log — the findings pack says it is open and the log says where it went."}
